      "sha256": "3ec3db703f2faf130498c66a5faa82b2fef5b24d4c7b520d54023ccfdd3285e4",
      "kind": "figure",
      "alt": "Figure 1. Codelets attach helpers to regions of code. Helpers are displayed inline with the rest of the code without obscuring it. This Codelet creates a jQuery Mobile button. Its helper is interactive and allows its user to customize the button by interacting with a form, drawing a line to illustrate which region of code each form element is changing. The user may also edit the code and the form will automatically update itself."
    },
    {
      "path": "figures/oney-codelets-chi2012/figure-002-p003.png",
