      "kind": "figure",
      "alt": "Figure 8. For consistency, Codelets have a standard mechanism for displaying warnings with text and any number of buttons. Helpers can take advantage of their semantic understanding of what their attached example code is supposed to do to display warnings even if the code is syntactically correct. This Codelet, for reading a file in Java, displays an error because the programmer has not specified a filename."
